 "_doc": "Msukaligwa Local Municipality (Ermelo), one account with three electricity meters (two kWh registers and a 'K' kVA meter), two prints. Print A (7 bills): 'TAX INVOICE' with a Property Information row (street, deposit), a Meter Information table (columns often garbled in the text, so readings are not taken) and Afrikaans 'Billing Information' lines 'DESC units tariff charges VAT total'; electricity = every 'ELEC BUSINESS' line (energy and the K-meter demand line, which the bill prices at the energy rate) + 'ELEK DIENS FOOI' (service fee -> other_r). The demand line is the ELEC BUSINESS line whose units equal the K meter's consumption (back-reference), falling back to the line with units < 100 when the meter table is garbled (1 bill). Print B (3 bills, 2 are the same June statement): newer Munsoft ledger with comma decimals; 'ELEC CONSUMPTION (KWH)' plus two '(KVA)'-labelled lines - the one with real readings [a to b] is the main kWh register (rate equal to the energy rate) and is counted as energy, the '[0 to n]' one is demand; the June print has ex-VAT Debit + VAT columns, the April print has VAT-inclusive Debit and the ex-VAT figure only in the detail rows' Exclusive column (used). Units with 3+ decimals are rebuilt via concat with a literal '.' from the bill. No service fee appears on print B. Fingerprint: the municipality's VAT number + name/web domain. Identity (--identity msk_identity_r, print A only): Total column - VAT column per electricity line vs the Charges column: 0.00 on 7/7; print B has no independent figure (VAT % not printed) so its 3 bills are circular (identity blank). Checks 0. Checked on all 10 bills."
}